WEBVTT

00:17.879 --> 00:24.285
1983, on a Sunday afternoon, sunlight slanting

00:24.325 --> 00:30.631
through the curtains of the living room. I was

00:30.751 --> 00:37.096
sitting at the upright, hands upon the keys. You

00:37.157 --> 00:41.000
pulled up a wooden chair and rested your guitar

00:41.080 --> 00:46.257
across your knees. No microphones, no stages,

00:46.297 --> 00:49.778
just a brother and a sister in the quiet air

00:51.599 --> 00:55.241
Finding out that every single note was lighter

00:56.041 --> 00:59.222
when we both were there

01:00.703 --> 01:06.285
By 85, the cousins came knocking at the door

01:07.066 --> 01:11.319
Tyler had his childhood drum kit Right across

01:11.359 --> 01:15.662
the basement floor. Evan plugged the bass in and

01:15.702 --> 01:19.845
the floorboard started shaking with a brand new

01:20.725 --> 01:24.168
beat. And in 86 we bought that second hand 84

01:24.468 --> 01:29.892
synth from down the street. Six and analog

01:29.992 --> 01:35.696
voices glowing blue and red in the dark. That was

01:35.756 --> 01:42.961
the night The engine caught the spark From an

01:42.981 --> 01:49.766
upright piano And a six-string amplifier We

01:49.826 --> 01:57.011
built a sanctuary Out of melody and fire Before

01:57.071 --> 02:03.536
the record labels Before the stadium lights It

02:03.576 --> 02:08.819
was just the five of us through those Virginia

02:08.959 --> 02:14.643
nights. No matter how far out into the stars we

02:14.683 --> 02:23.369
fly, I'm still sitting right beside you as the

02:23.449 --> 02:24.590
years go by.

02:39.173 --> 02:43.336
Holly at the kitchen table With her notebook

02:43.416 --> 02:49.360
spread around Drawing up battle plans For a

02:49.480 --> 02:55.163
homemade family sound We didn't need a fortune

02:56.004 --> 03:02.448
We already had the gold Five kids in a basement

03:02.928 --> 03:10.491
With a story to be told From an upright piano and a

03:10.511 --> 03:16.333
six-string amplifier We built a sanctuary

03:17.013 --> 03:23.414
out of melody and fire Before the record labels,

03:23.854 --> 03:29.276
before the stadium lights It was just the five of

03:29.496 --> 03:35.219
us through those Virginia nights No matter how

03:35.359 --> 03:42.462
far out into the stars we fly I'm still sitting

03:42.562 --> 03:49.005
right beside you As the years go by

03:55.724 --> 03:56.849
you

04:15.939 --> 04:20.742
Now we have every instrument That money could

04:20.842 --> 04:28.085
ever buy A fortress in the mountains Underneath

04:28.185 --> 04:33.668
an open sky But when I close my eyes And let the

04:33.848 --> 04:38.511
static fade away We're back on that piano bench

04:40.011 --> 04:40.832
In 1983 Today

04:47.755 --> 04:52.676
From an upright piano and a six-string

04:52.856 --> 04:59.558
amplifier, we built a sanctuary out of melody

04:59.838 --> 05:05.459
and fire. Before the record labels, before the

05:05.499 --> 05:10.781
stadium lights, it was just the five of us.

05:11.161 --> 05:16.262
Through those Virginia nights, no matter how

05:16.382 --> 05:24.345
far Into the stars we fly I'm still sitting right

05:24.425 --> 05:26.625
beside you

05:29.126 --> 05:33.368
As the years go by

05:37.229 --> 05:39.570
Right beside you on the bench

05:43.005 --> 05:46.923
Where the music began

